{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world","id":1454025,"title":"Which clan is the most dangerous in the modern world?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-01T18:07:45-07:00","id":1454025,"title":"Which clan is the most dangerous in the modern world?","content":"Considering everything: ability to influence mortals, ability to detect ambushes, ability to conduct ambushes, utility, single combat ability, least crippling bane, etc.<br /> <br /> Note that this is NOT the kind of thread where you say things like &quot;this can has the most influence, this other clan has the best combat ability&quot;. It's assumed that not all abilities are of equal value in the modern nights, and that some discipline sets synergize internally better than others.<br /> <br /> Rather, which clan is the most complete package to survive and thrive in the modern nights?<br /> <br /> I'd nominate the Toreador: great influence discipline, great combat discipline, great discipline for detecting ambushes and learning secrets. Great synergy between Auspex and other two Disciplines, in that detecting ambushes and learning secrets and having a get-out-of-dodge power is perfect for when you've detected that bomb or 50 caliber sniper rifle. Presence is perfect for exploiting those political secrets you've learned. Bane is more a nuisance than crippling. Lacking in stealth and brawling ability, but that's more a nuisance than crippling in the age of sniper rifles and explosives. In many ways these creatures are just made for the modern world.<br /> <br /> Your nomination?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T19:26:20-07:00","id":1454033,"title":"","content":"So, yadda yadda yadda, different tables, different results, varies by edition, blah.<br /> <br /> <b>Vysha's Flawlessly Perfect Strategy for Surviving the Modern Nights</b> states the following, in order of importance (in V20 at least, less familiar with V5):<br /> 1) It is always better to avoid a fight than to win a fight.<br /> 2) It is always better to defuse a fight than to win a fight.<br /> 3) It is always better to escape a fight than to win a fight.<br /> 4) It is always better to survive a fight than to win a fight.<br /> <br /> For surviving and thriving the modern nights, no clan can beat the Toreador, because their discipline spread allows them to fulfill 1-3 within their discipline spread. Auspex allows for a greater chance of noting danger well before it reaches the kindred, allowing them to just simply go somewhere else. Presence hits the sweet spot for #2, allowing them to make an enemy a friend, or at least scare them away. Both Celerity and Presence give great escape avenues, through Dread Gaze penalties to an enemy and Celerity to GTFO faster.<br /> <br /> But that's all baseline, using disciplines as vanilla as can be. Other clans have discipline spreads that can be applied in cunning and unusual ways for equal or greater effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Surgeon General's Warning: Vysha's Flawlessly Perfect Strategy for Surviving the Modern Nights is only a treatment, not a cure. See your Storyteller if VFPSfStMN is right for you. Side effects may include Willpower and Blood Point drain, cowardice, itchy scalp and ghoul meat shield armies.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:00:37-07:00","id":1454039,"title":"","content":"Malvakians are a strong contender for me. My general assessment is, like Vysha's, one that stresses avoiding fights over winning them. The Auspex, Dominate (Or Dementation since edition wasn't specified), and Obfuscate are a solid set for information gathering and avoiding problems rather than tackling them head on.<br /> <br /> Weakness/Bane/etc.is something that I think actually plays into the Malks' favor in modern nights. A lot of the Clans have drawbacks that have only gotten more difficult to compensate for in modern nights compared to ancient ones (or are fairly time-neutral). Malks are one of the few Clans were their drawback is actually less of a problem on average as the mainstream acceptance and accommodation of mental health problems has grown steadily. While far from where we'd society to be in that regard, modern times in developed countries means a much more sympathetic human population (and younger vampires) than 50 years ago. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:36:34-07:00","id":1454045,"title":"","content":"My first suggestion needs to get off their &quot;rawr I'm so evil and inhuman!&quot; high horse first: Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Auspex speaks for itself, really.<br /> <br /> Animalism, on the other hand...let's just say nobody's ever gone broke making viral animal and pet videos on the internet. Animalism is your one-stop shop for making sure Fluffy does the cute thing that gets those clicks and engagement...and if the thing is too complex for Fluffy? possess it!<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is the unspoken horror of a modern nights setting, if Tzimisce would ever stop doing evil shit with it and actually give a think towards how it could be used for, hell I don't know...black market plastic surgery? just work the Vicissitude magic while the patient is under, and maybe a drop or two of blood to keep them coming back for more.<br /> <br /> But really, the crown in my mind goes to two bloodlines, depending how you want to play it: the Zantosa and the Telyavs. Both bloodlines are Toreador on bath salts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:50:31-07:00","id":1454047,"title":"","content":"I'd agree regarding the Malkavians, with the addition that basically no one can reliably predict what they're going to <i>do</i>, individually or collectively. That uncertainty makes them incredibly dangerous in a society that's largely static and hidebound. They may not be tops in terms of physical power, influence, wealth, what have you, but in dealing with them everyone else is at a disadvantage because they're generally forced to be reactive rather than proactive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T00:11:33-07:00","id":1454052,"title":"","content":"I would vote for <b>Venture </b>form a setting perspective.<br /> <br /> It has less to do with their disciplines and bane then their culture and place.<br /> <br /> I would argue that powerful CEOs, rich folk and politicians run the show. Even more so in WOD. The Venture are just most represented in that segment of society.<br /> <br /> They do not fight you personally. They might not even decide to crush you. They probably do not even know you.<br /> <br /> <b>They have created a system that crushes people like you and elevates them.</b><br /> <br /> For a PC - join team malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 07-02-2021, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T01:28:48-07:00","id":1454054,"title":"","content":"the issue is that most clans are dangerous for different reasons, a ventrue and a malk are going to ruin your life but through completely different methodes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T03:35:19-07:00","id":1454063,"title":"","content":"I think that's where the &quot;modern nights&quot; factor helps narrow things down. My own suggestion of Malkavians dropped considerably down the list if we change ears. An era where there's a much harsher stigma against mental illness means their drawback hits a lot harder around the kine. In an era where public violence is more &quot;acceptable&quot; their lack of affinity for physical Disciplines limits them. Vampires are, by their nature, all dangerous. But the kinds of dangerous they are can ebb and flow regarding the current state of affairs and how adaptable they are.<br /> <br /> Venture are dangerous, but their very lopsided towards social power. Fortitude is nice, but as it tends to go, not being hit is better than being able to take a hit. In an era where information is even more powerful than ever, lacking the more covert intelligence gathering abilities you can find in Auspex, Animalism, some forms of Necrmancy/Oblivion, or the stealth of Obfuscate of Protean to boost mundane surveillance, is a pretty big drawback.<br /> <br /> To use a less modern example, consider the strategic issues the Allies faced when the Enigma Machine was cracked. On one hand, they suddenly had a massive upper hand because they had access to all that thought-to-be-secure information, on the other hand they didn't want the Germans to realize the machine was cracked so it would keep being used. <br /> <br /> More specialist/focused Clans like the Venture and Brujah don't really have a lot of flexibility. Without the edge in the cat and mouse game of using enough information to defeat your enemies without them realizing how you're doing it, they're force to lean in hard on attacking directly and trying to finish it before their enemies can retreat and reassess. They basically have to announce that they broken the Enigma Machine, and hope that they can do enough damage before it's replaced that it was worth it. The Clans that offer a more flexible package in information warfare can play a longer game.<br /> <br /> That's the sort of consideration I think lets us create reasonable arguments for Clans to have an edge in a specific context. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T05:38:47-07:00","id":1454067,"title":"","content":"City Gangrel with their Celerity, Obsfucate and Protean discipline spread spring to mind. They can hide anywhere as anything to tracking them down is almost impossible. I'd say they would be the best survivors, but they're not naturally suited to ruling the world. The Followers of Set are always solid, Obsfucate, Presence and Serpentis. Obsfucate keeps them alive, Presence lets them manipulate people and Serpentis is kind of a grab-bag discipline that helps them both offensively and defensively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T06:20:43-07:00","id":1454072,"title":"","content":"We need to know in what edition of the game. But unsurprising I think, pre-v5, it's...<br /> <br /> Tremere.<br /> <br /> Too many overpower rituals and paths, which protect against almost everything! Technology, chimerstry, foes coming from umbra, presence, mortal hunters, spirits, obtenebration, ghosts, faes, ghouls, garou, fera, AND mages/true magick. Path of Blood have the potential to nullifies Dominate (the 2nd strongest discipline in the entire game) if the cainite raise her generation on a daily basis. If nothing else goes well the Cainite can simply teleport to their refuge or a friend<br /> <br /> On top of that, clan tremere, at least before v5 bs, is the most cooperative clan in the entire game (through cheating, of course). <br /> <br /> If we are going to discuss disciplines as the main factor, Tremere have completely broken rituals like &quot;Blade of the Forbidden Flower&quot; and many other ways to replicate many disciplines, like obfuscate and daimonion. The clan has possibly the best combination of disciplines in the game, as they have the two strongest disciplines plus an A tier discipline.<br /> <br /> Why I didn't pick Malkavians: <br /> <br /> Dementation is a discipline that has been greatly weakened in v20, as the madness inflicted can be cured with the expenditure of Willpower and therapy. I think it only gets strong from level 7. Plus, I have a very different impression of psychological illnesses. The Clan flaw, as I see it, is not some silly eccentricity like collecting a bunch of stereotypically cute things or having two personalities where one is a femme fatale and the other is a business woman. But I'm not going to get into discussion about this, lest derail the thread.<br /> <br /> Special mention: Assamite. Alamut is a very safe place for sure. Additionally, Quietus has the power to purify the target of any mystical influence, making it very difficult to utilize infiltration strategies by ghouls or mortals controlled by disciplines and other intrigues.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: If you use ninth level Chimerstry on a victim, the victim is transported to an inaccessible private dimension. If she is an willing victim and don't try to escape, she can live there for an indefinite amount of time, obviously not being able to be murdered.<br /> <br /> Malkavian: Many friends around the world, disciplines that make you an oracle and, at advanced levels, can allow you to stay alive (more or less) even after being murdered.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T08:40:48-07:00","id":1454080,"title":"","content":"Modern Nights? I\u2019ll vote Caitiff. No specific weakness to worry about, start with three disciplines you can improve without a teacher that don\u2019t have to fit any pattern (auspex, dominate, protean? Why not?). Sure, it\u2019ll take a little more xp to buy those up, but you\u2019ve got a price break on all the others and your fellow underclass Caitiff will have those in aggregate so it\u2019s easier to pick up a suite of the common disciplines without stepping on interclan rivalries.<br /> <br /> Sure, the elders and clan iconoclasts hate you, but they hate everybody; they just don\u2019t have to pretend with you. And there can be advantages to playing out the role of underdog as long as you don\u2019t overdo it.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also relatively young and so more accustomed by nature to the modern world and don\u2019t have any particular clan baggage weighing them down.<br /> <br /> So, overall Caitiffs are probably most adaptable to the Modern Nights IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T09:08:22-07:00","id":1454084,"title":"","content":"I think I'll tentatively put my money on the Banu Haqim, followed by the Tremere. They have one big drawback in common in current times, the organizing structure of their Clans being broken apart; the Tremere also suffer from just about everyone else hating their guts.<br /> <br /> But we are talking about two Clans with organization and collective resources. Both Clans have access to Blood Magic and Auspex (depends on caste and edition for BH). Tremere also get Dominate, which includes the ability to alter memories, excellent for manipulating intelligence and protecting the Masquerade. Banu Haqim gets just about everything through their caste system, which gives them a flexibility most other Clans don't have.<br /> <br /> I can't recall the current situation with the BH Bane, but the Tremere Bane in V5 seems pretty *shrug* to me. Is a blood bond really necessary when you can read minds, brainwash people, and do almost anything with magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T08:05:54-07:00","id":1454134,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dangerous&quot; is a word that means something, and it's not a synonym for &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;powerful&quot; or &quot;beloved by the author.&quot;. Something is dangerous if it can and is likely to do you harm if you fiddle with it. Dangerous is the blank space in this modified saying about Disney: &quot;You fuck with __________, they fuck with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think the modern nights changes anything here: I think the obvious answers are Gangrel and Tzimisce, with Brujah in a very close second.`<br /> <br /> (I can, however, understand why someone would say Assamites or Tremere.)","signature":"\"Dangerous\" is a word that means something, and it's not a synonym for \"cool\" or \"powerful\" or \"beloved by the author.\". Something is dangerous if it can and is likely to do you harm if you fiddle with it. Dangerous is the blank space in this modified saying about Disney: \"You fuck with __________, they fuck with you.\"<br /> <br /> I don't think the modern nights changes anything here: I think the obvious answers are Gangrel and Tzimisce, with Brujah in a very close second.`<br /> <br /> (I can, however, understand why someone would say Assamites or Tremere.)","edited":{"userid":13136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","user":"Legendre","date":". 07-03-2021, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T12:39:01-07:00","id":1454148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1454134#post1454134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dangerous&quot; is a word that means something, and it's not a synonym for &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;powerful&quot; or &quot;beloved by the author.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone being saying something to the contrary? Though power and danger tend to go together as being dangerous is a form of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something is dangerous if it can and is likely to do you harm if you fiddle with it. </div> </div> </div>Where does the &quot;if you fiddle with it,&quot; qualifier come from? A hurricane is dangerous regardless of any personal actions someone takes that might &quot;fiddle&quot; with it. Vampires are extremely dangerous without needing to be provoked. If you're not a vampire, you're either food, a pawn, or a threat to be eliminated... all of that means they're going to try to harm you or put you in harm's way. If you're a vampire.... well actually the same criteria basically apply to similar results. A low generation vampire isn't fiddling with other vampires even though a good number of them are considering how to eat said vampire and lower their own generation.<br /> <br /> As well you seem oddly focused on direct physical harm rather than the broader definition of harm that leads of a broader usage of dangerous. Fucking with Disney doesn't mean you're going to literally have Mickey show up and break your leg. It means they're going to sue you (farther) into poverty and then take the chance to exert their power and further twist the laws in their favor to let them do the same to the next person in their cross hairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the modern nights changes anything here: I think the obvious answers are Gangrel and Tzimisce, with Brujah in a very close second.`<br /> <br /> (I can, however, understand why someone would say Assamites or Tremere.) </div> </div> </div>Here's why the modern night's matter:<br /> <br /> Your Gangrel with their Protean and Fortitude is certainly a nasty customer in a stand-up hand-to-hand fight. But that means they're either extremely limited by the needs of the Masquerade (monster claws are obviously supernatural, and tanking lots of seemingly deadly wounds is as well), or putting themselves in danger to be dangerous.<br /> <br /> But who's going to play fair to that when you don't have to? And modern nights means modern technology to help you fight unfair (aka smart). All that hand-to-hand monstrosity means nothing if someone can just stealth-kite you from a distance with guns and specialized ammunition so your Gangrel's in torpor before they can even figure out where the attack is coming from.<br /> <br /> Modern technology (and reality if the Masquerade is going to come into the situation) + smart use of subtle Disciplines is more dangerous than being a physical powerhouse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T13:53:19-07:00","id":1454153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1454134#post1454134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dangerous&quot; is a word that means something, and it's not a synonym for &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;powerful&quot; or &quot;beloved by the author.&quot;. Something is dangerous if it can and is likely to do you harm if you fiddle with it. Dangerous is the blank space in this modified saying about Disney: &quot;You fuck with __________, they fuck with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think the modern nights changes anything here: I think the obvious answers are Gangrel and Tzimisce, with Brujah in a very close second.`<br /> <br /> (I can, however, understand why someone would say Assamites or Tremere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>the problem i see here is that you seem to only consider phisical harm and not other forms of harm like social, financial and mental harm","signature":"\"Dangerous\" is a word that means something, and it's not a synonym for \"cool\" or \"powerful\" or \"beloved by the author.\". Something is dangerous if it can and is likely to do you harm if you fiddle with it. Dangerous is the blank space in this modified saying about Disney: \"You fuck with __________, they fuck with you.\"<br /> <br /> I don't think the modern nights changes anything here: I think the obvious answers are Gangrel and Tzimisce, with Brujah in a very close second.`<br /> <br /> (I can, however, understand why someone would say Assamites or Tremere.)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T13:54:03-07:00","id":1454154,"title":"","content":"For my two cents, I would say the Tremere are the most dangerous clan in V20 and earlier versions.<br /> <br /> As others have stated, the combination of Thaumaturgy &amp; Dominate more or less gives that a massive lead in power. The fact that they have Auspex means they can collect large amounts of information as well as protect themselves from any Obfuscate based clan. The Rituals and the variety of Paths means that even if you don't have the right knowledge on hand, the clan solidarity means you can more that likely put in a call to have a specialist temporarily assigned to your chantry until the problem has passed.<br /> <br /> The chantries are described as routinely being able to withstand centuries worth of warfare from multiple clans. Thus it is safe to say that when bunkered down the Tremere are one of the hardest clans to actually get at. Even then the Tremere often have artificial minions in their chantries so they are one of the few clans with more than human/animals ghouls at their beck and call.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are better hackers than the nosferatu thanks to the path of Technomancy. Thus any thing that is dependent on computers is weak to the clan or can be put to their uses. Money is a non-issue for them since they can just produce their equipment with Path of Conjuration or just produce precut gemstones and sell that for money online. With a big enough bank account the clan can play in the same sandbox as the Ventrue, the Giovanni, or the Lasombra when it comes to business influence. <br /> <br /> The Tremere clans biggest weaknesses are two things specifically.<br /> <br /> The first is that because of the clans focus on the arcane, they have very stringent standards for who can be embraced or ghouled. While this means a higher baseline of quality control for neonates, it also means that they can't replace losses quickly or easily. This is part of the reason the clan relies on Gargoyles and other artificial minions for front line duty as well as defaulting to &quot;bunker down&quot; and outlast the siege mentality.<br /> <br /> The second issue that the Tremere have is that the writers can not stop tinkering with the clan, its backstory, its metagame placement, etc. If you compare the Tremere to pretty much every other clan, they have had more fluff related twists, more characters responsible for pivotal moments, and more plot points than any other group. Is San Francisco being invaded by Kuei-jin, call in the tremere to contain them, do you need the plot point containment to be breached, a tremere character is canonically a traitor. Do you need the assamites/banu haquim hobbled, call the Tremere in. Do you need Saulot to do something, have the sabbat Tremere immolate for no good reason. It goes on and on, the Tremere have been treated as plot filler so many times that it's laughable. Then of course the Tremere were introduced as the only clan to have magic, but then the writers started giving magic to every new clan or clan update. Yeah the writers are truely the Tremeres only real enemy.<br /> <br /> It is arguable that the only clan that comes close to the meta-power or meta-influence of the Tremere on the setting is the Baali for their supposed corruption of some other clans and their max level disciplines can unleash WoD brand Cthulhu on the setting. Alternatively the Giovanni could do something similar by bringing down the barriers to the lands of the dead, but the critical thing to remember is that in the case of the Tremere they have done these things already, while the Giovanni and Baali are largely just potential plot points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T15:09:59-07:00","id":1454158,"title":"","content":"The Tremere Thaum advantage is one of the most edition dependent ones, which makes it very variable. In 1e or 5e, Thaumaturgy isn't that sprawling mess of a platter of powers. In 2e it's definitely at its height of that matter, but in Rev. and V20 there was a very conscious effort to dilute the Tremere's Thaum Edge by having lots of blood sorceries out there besides them that can easily rival them in power. The Assamite trio gives the Tremere a solid bit of competition regarding internal Clan cooperation to leverage a bunch of specialists with broad access to a lot of different powers.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Assamites are also a Clan that gets a lot of attention from the writers, and generally to their detriment in terms of their potential ranking in this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T15:51:55-07:00","id":1454159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1454052#post1454052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would vote for <b>Venture </b>form a setting perspective.<br /> <br /> It has less to do with their disciplines and bane then their culture and place.<br /> <br /> I would argue that powerful CEOs, rich folk and politicians run the show. Even more so in WOD. The Venture are just most represented in that segment of society.<br /> <br /> They do not fight you personally. They might not even decide to crush you. They probably do not even know you.<br /> <br /> <b>They have created a system that crushes people like you and elevates them.</b><br /> <br /> For a PC - join team malkavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's the Ventrue as well. They're not only the most dangerous when provoked, they're *actively causing the most harm* through late stage capitalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T01:02:58-07:00","id":1454180,"title":"","content":"Dominate malkavians and Ventrue are big screwers, but the Toreador really up them in terms of numbers. Malkaviand and especially Ventrue are more elite clans where each member needs an amount of investment. Toreador powerset works for just about any tom, dick or harry, they are supurbly generalist. Each Ventrue can do more damage than a single Toreador, but there are probably about three times more Toreador than Ventrue. <br /> <br /> No physical disciplines/fortitude is kinda good in a world with modern weaponry. You dont need much potence to win against mortals and celerity doesnt compare so well to full auto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T09:01:39-07:00","id":1454207,"title":"","content":"Remember that clan numbers are dependent on getting permission to embrace for most clans. Which clan includes the most princes who are the ones giving that permission? Spoiler alert: it's not the Toreador.<br /> <br /> Obviously that doesn't do much to restrict the numbers of clans like Brujah and Gangrel, but they generally aren't competing in the same arena and have to face higher attrition rates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T06:59:33-07:00","id":1454278,"title":"","content":"I recall a book stating Toreador come in at second for number of princes. They're a clan of Queens after all. The Toreador are far more likely to go Anarch than the Ventrue. Far more likely to embrace on a whim and think of the consequences later, and have a very good generalist discipline set. In evolution, generalists win out. You should also consider that the Ventrue will embrace usually on a group decision. Someone'll suggest it at the board, and maybe they'll argue about it before making a decision. Maybe Ron won't embrace because Jonah's canidate is more promising at this moment and they really want to do this collectively to avoid favours... The Toreador don't have that unity. If multiple Toreador want to embrace then it's all down to who can convince the prince and offer the best favours. The Toreador have some soft power in influencing who among them gets to embrace, but they don't have the iron grasp that the ventrue do in making sure what's best for the clan appears. As such, if we assume the prince is from a third clan, the Toreador will be far more plentiful than the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T14:15:08-07:00","id":1454302,"title":"","content":"In current nights? I vote Nosferatu. Nossies took an hit with ShreckNet collapsing but at the end of the day they still control information, and i the WoD knowing where your enemies are, who do they eat and how to get them is generally more important than calling yourself \u201cthe prince\u201d. Ventrues put a lot of stock in titles but, as the Lasombra say, power and titles don\u2019t always go together, information on the other hand is power, in the WoD especially so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T14:28:19-07:00","id":1454304,"title":"","content":"Vampire demographic is such a hard thing to really generalize about I'm not sure this goes somewhere fruitful. Most cities have too small a population of vampires to really care about whatever the &quot;global&quot; view of the Clans looks like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1454278#post1454278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In evolution, generalists win out</div> </div> </div> </div>Not... really how evolution works.<br /> <br /> The way evolution really applies to this conversation is more direct anyway: humans are a highly successful generalist species, and vampires have to cope with human behavioral patterns. Generalist vampires have an edge over specialist vampires because of how broad human behaviors can be as generalists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:29:50-07:00","id":1454317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1454278#post1454278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall a book stating Toreador come in at second for number of princes. They're a clan of Queens after all. The Toreador are far more likely to go Anarch than the Ventrue. Far more likely to embrace on a whim and think of the consequences later, and have a very good generalist discipline set. In evolution, generalists win out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Selection pressures may vary. Consult your ecological niches before beginning vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:49:34-07:00","id":1454320,"title":"","content":"I would not underestimate the Toreadors. Indeed they may in appearance look less powerful than the other patrician clan of the Camarilla (Ventrue and Tremere). But they also lack any real enemy unlike them. Such as the Brujah or the Tzimice to mention the most obvious one.<br /> <br /> Also the Ventrue and Tremere fates is deeply woven into the success of the Camarilla. And should the organisation fail for some reason, they status would fall greatly just like we've seen with the complete collapse of the Lasombra after their defection.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Toreador already enjoy possess a certain status in both the Anarch and the Sabbat. One of their own even was the Sabbat's regent for a time. True the Toreador are less prominent in those sects but that can easily change with enough defection. Defection that will as well be taken with more ease and less apprehension than if it was a Ventrue or a Tremere.<br /> <br /> And finally the Toreador still have their antediluvian. And in the end, that maybe the only thing that matters. All other clans that aspire for leadership: Ventrue, Tremere, Tzimice, Lasombra, and even Brujah have either their antediluvian removed from the Jihad or should rightfully fear their wrath after some... unfortunate events during the first Anarch Revolt.<br /> Meanwhile the Toreadors may still hope to enjoy Arikel protection when Gehenna comes. Or not, but that's still more than many.<br /> <br /> Toreadors are really the diplomats/grey eminence clan by excellence. They may not always enjoy the benefits of being the most influential clan. But such position has its downside as well. Sometimes it's better to pull the strings behind the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 07-05-2021, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T09:53:15-07:00","id":1454353,"title":"","content":"I am not sure about the ventrue embracing a lot becuase they are very pragmatic on the matter , Lodin for example only embraced becuase the people he choose had a particular set of skills he needed (Lorraine is the exception).<br /> <br /> Also they are very competitive so while they can cooperate they will rarely get along , continuating with Lodin example he exterminated all ventrue in chicago area becuase he view them as rivals once he ascended to power and half his progeny exist to act as rivals so his progeny doesnt rebel against him.<br /> <br /> And we cannot either forget that the ventrue capacity to embrace can be limited by other clans and primogens as happened again with Lodin and it makes sense becuase if a clan starts embracing a lot it will be likely to win in a war against other clans who logically wouldn\u00b4t let that happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 07-06-2021, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:06:06-07:00","id":1454356,"title":"","content":"Ventrue... because well... you know they flex. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T12:20:23-07:00","id":1454474,"title":"","content":"In modern nights the Toreador. Social engineering, media control, gaining attention and fame is everything today. And also I\u2019m imagining a Toreador social media influencer despite the heavy danger that presents and a Nosfurtu V-Tuber","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T18:42:46-07:00","id":1454491,"title":"","content":"Hey guys---new here obviously but 1 more vote for Tremere being the most &quot;realistically dangerous&quot; of the clans. Most, if not all would be highly intelligent people embraced into the clan, then you have this incredible combo of disciplines/powers; blood sorcery, dominate and auspex. With high levels of those powers, and most of the clan tending to be on the same page one way or another... + incredible &quot;home base defense&quot; with the various magical wards and gargoyle minions, and perhaps some blood-bound human servants as day-time protectors.... At least *realistically*, a group like this could easily end up dominating this world from behind the scenes if they wanted to go that route. (*I imagine they would be the type to ally themselves with powerful world leaders and all related staff/cabinets, etc., ultimately using them like puppets....ensuring that everything works out to the benefit of clan Tremere in one way or another.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26933-vulgar-impostor","name":"Vulgar Impostor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T05:03:22-07:00","id":1455024,"title":"","content":"I vote Nosferatu due to fact that no matter what happens, who is in power etc. - everyone needs Nosferatu, their information gathering network, their assassins, spies and they rule underworld and underworld is big in every big city. Imo Nossies are most likely to survive no matter what shift in power there is.<br /> <br /> Setites are also worth to mention. They don't flex the power like Ventrue or combat like Brujah. Yet they are everywhere, united and infiltrate tons of big organizations. They are like Hydra from MCU.<br /> <br /> Ventrue could be next choice but they flex too much. Toreadors imo are better for reasons mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T17:49:41-07:00","id":1455772,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu hands down. If the Gangrel and/or Tzimisce joined, doubly so.<br /> <br /> Here's how it plays out:<br /> <br /> Modern Era has Blockchain tech which will be used for Global Identification.<br /> <br /> Central Bank Digital Currency will be tracked and any goods of importance will be attached to NFTs.<br /> <br /> Biometric tracking will be in just about all cameras and devices.<br /> <br /> Algos will hunt for any 'illegal' commercial activity.<br /> <br /> All the Clans that rely upon humans as proxies as well as hunting in populated areas will be at terrible disadvantage.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu can live far underground, sustain themselves upon animals and largely don't need human affairs to keep power.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu, Gangrel, and Tzimisce team up, show the SI they aren't much of a threat to Humanity, then sell the other clans out.<br /> <br /> The Tremere will need too much blood and willpower to last for long. The Vienna Chantry showed blood magic doesn't stop day time ordinance.<br /> <br /> The Social Clans will literally leave trails anytime they go in public or use personal assets. Algos will eventually tie ghouls to 'suspicious' spending.<br /> <br /> So Clans will have to bargain with the SI but knowing how they infiltrate human organizations, it will be no, or a very raw deal. Nosferatu will coach SI on how to defend against kindred tactics.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu cut a deal in exchange for survival they will keep their population fixed, help humans in areas that humans can't travel, and help the Technocracy move on.<br /> <br /> The End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T05:52:51-07:00","id":1455793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454025-which-clan-is-the-most-dangerous-in-the-modern-world?p=1455772#post1455772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern Era has Blockchain tech which will be used for Global Identification.<br /> <br /> Central Bank Digital Currency will be tracked and any goods of importance will be attached to NFTs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of assumptions here. While blockchain encrypted IDs might replace other systems for day-to-day personal identity verification, very few experts in the field think it's a remotely good idea for any government to actually get rid of systems that are easier to prove in-person we that's better. Blockchain IDs might be great for users and companies (and even governments for providing paid services) as a more secure and speedy way to connect a real person to a digital communication in a trustworthy fashion, but it's highly unlikely we'll got to the blockchain tech for your basic government IDs like drivers licenses.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of debate about whether central banks should even be getting into the digital currency market, and if so when that should happen, and how to implement it. NFTs are not particularly valuable to central banks because central banks have no particular use for non-fungible items. The whole point of a central bank is to manage a fungible asset's value and distribution. <br /> <br /> Even if everything does got in this direction (also the thread is about now, not in 10 years), that doesn't mean non-governmental cryptocurrency is just going to disappear for whoever wants something that isn't setup to be easily searched by the government. And cryptocurrencies are a mixed bag here. They're actually pretty good at fending off broad sweeping algorithms because there's just too much noise to connection any given transaction to a specific user on a fishing expedition. They're horrible at stopping someone that's specifically looking for a known user's transaction history We're very far from algorithms being capable of just flagging cryptocurrency transactions as suspicious by just unleashing them on Internet. However, we're very much already at the point where cryptocurrencies aren't going to stop the government from finding your money just because you don't use a bank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the Clans that rely upon humans as proxies as well as hunting in populated areas will be at terrible disadvantage. </div> </div> </div>Not... really? Digital currencies make vampire's lives easier and less reliant on human proxies the more automated they are. Right now, a vampire doesn't need a ghoul's living identity to open up a Bitcoin wallet, and use it to handle all of their basic transactions for maintaining their lifestyles and havens; beyond having to transfer Bitcoins to a ghoul to pay any remaining in-person services like a plumber.<br /> <br /> The only real disadvantage here is that the Nosferatu were arbitrarily made the &quot;hacker&quot; Clan that adapted to the digital era better than the rest. However in 2021, most neonates are going to be digital natives, not anachronistic old folks that remember when the telegraph was fancy new tech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nosferatu can live far underground, sustain themselves upon animals and largely don't need human affairs to keep power. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Far underground,&quot; is kinda meaningless... esp. since animals large enough to feed on don't live far underground.<br /> <br /> You seem to be, without directly stating it, that this is really all about Animalism. But that doesn't really have the impact it could. Pre-V5, Animalism wasn't necessary to feed exclusively on animals, and you could even fill your blood pool completely without it. Pre-V5 relies way too much on social stigma over rules to stop vampires from avoiding human blood all together. In V5, Animalism lost it's best feeding power: Beckoning. Animalism used to be able to bring animals too you; making it easy to get your undead hands on some larger critters that are actually worth some vitae. V5 Animalism lacks that, which means you lose a lot of the &quot;live underground&quot; stuff when you have to go hunt your meals anyway.<br /> <br /> You're also skipping (while not a knock against the Nosferatu) Obfuscate here. V5 Obfuscate specifically getting you the ability to mess with electronic devices takes a giant chunk out of the threat of biometrics everywhere. Auspex + Dominate + Obfuscation = super easy to get people to not be suspicious as they follow your nondescript self to somewhere away from digital eyes (and eventually you can just Conceal your car and it will be equally protected from notice on digital security systems) and then feed and drive your victim somewhere depending on your methods without having to worry about computers figuring you out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nosferatu cut a deal in exchange for survival they will keep their population fixed... </div> </div> </div>This is pretty far fetched, and there's no particular reason the SI is going to care about this. Every Clan is smart enough to realize that the second all the other Clans are dead, the SI will turn on them and all they did was doom vampires completely, not survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}